 First, we need to calculate the area of the plot in square centimeters using the dimensions provided in the triangle and the rectangle. Then, we convert the area from square centimeters to square miles using the given scale (1 cm equals 2 miles). Finally, we convert square miles to acres. </think>
\[
\text{Area of the triangle} = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{height} = \frac{1}{2} \times 10 \times 10 = 50 \text{ square centimeters}
\]
\[
\text{Area of the rectangle} = \text{base} \times \text{height} = 15 \times 10 = 150 \text{ square centimeters}
\]
\[
\text{Total area in square centimeters} = 50 + 150 = 200 \text{ square centimeters}
\]
\[
\text{Scale: } 1 \text{ cm} = 2 \text{ miles} \implies 1 \text{ square cm} = (2)^2 = 4 \text{ square miles}
\]
\[
\text{Total area in square miles} = 200 \times 4 = 800 \text{ square miles}
\]
\[
\text{Total area in acres} = 800 \times 640 = 512,000 \text{ acres}
\]
\[
\boxed{512000}
\]

