Since $1~\text{cm} = 2 \text{ miles}$, therefore in the above diagram:
\begin{align*}
AB &= 15~\text{cm}=30~\text{miles} \\
BC &= 10~\text{cm} = 20~\text{miles}
\end{align*}
Since this from a figure, we get a right-angled triangle. Therefore
\begin{align*}
AC^2 &= 15^2 + 10^2 \\
&= 225 + 100 \\
&= 325
\end{align*}
By Pythagoras Theorem, $$AC=\sqrt{AC^2}=\sqrt{225 + 100} = \sqrt{325} \approx 18.027~\text{miles}$$
Since 1 square mile = 640 acres, therefore $$18.027~\text{miles}^2 \times 640 = 11535.744~\text{acres}$$ $\textbf{ (Thus 152 acres are in the plot.) }$ <answer> 11535.744 acres </answer>

